RF.put("questb:b79",{"8559":{"id":8559,"t":"Conqueror's Greaves","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of War, 5 Ivory Scarabs and 5 Gold Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj. This quest also requires Neutral faction with the Brood of Nozdormu.\nQiraji Bindings of Command Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of War Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"Qiraji magic is strong and ancient. The most powerful qiraji wield items of such might, they'd give pause even to a dragon.\nBring me the qiraji bindings of command and other minor components by and I'll create a set of powerful boots for you.\nYou will find them useful in the fight against the enemy.","rew":"You will receive:\nConqueror's Greaves\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. You've proven you're no ordinary mortal.\nI give you these with the confidence they'll aid you in crushing the vile qiraji.\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Warrior Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8559\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Conqueror's Greaves this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of War, 5 Ivory Scarabs and 5 Gold Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8639":{"id":8639,"t":"Deathdealer's Helm","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of the War, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nVek'lor's Diadem Emperor Vek'lor in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of War Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The Twin Emperors... their incessant whispers are slowly taking a toll on my sanity. They mock me, knowing I cannot step further into their domain to save my brother Arygos.\nIn my visions I see their monstrous faces adorned by powerful crowns. But I will have my revenge... I will transmute these symbols of Qiraji power to ones better suited to our needs.\nBring me the components I require, ‹name›. I will give you a headpiece of unmatched power.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathdealer's Helm\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring me the components I asked for, ‹name›?","done":"You've succeeded! The whispers from the Twin Emperors have ceased.\nTake this as a reward. The mere sight of it will strike fear in the hearts of the Qiraji... it shall remind them of their fallen leaders and of the mortal that slew them.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Rogue Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8639\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Deathdealer's Helm this quest\nBring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of the War, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"639":{"id":639,"t":"Sigil of Strom","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get the Sigil of Strom for Zengu in Hammerfall.\nSigil of Strom Syndicate Conjuror 3 % , Syndicate Magus 2 % , Syndicate Prowler 2 %","desc":"In ancient times, trolls fought against the Arathorian Empire and our most capable adversary, Lord Ignaeus of Strom, named Trollbane. He rode into battle wielding Trol'kalar--troll slayer, in their ancient tongue.\nBut now the sons of Trollbane are weakened, their stronghold brought to ruin.\nThe sword is protected by several sigils that were divided among the survivors of Stromgarde, and we must retrieve them.\nThe first was taken by the Syndicate, one of their men in Stromgarde should have it.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Have you located the first sigil yet? It is most likely carried on the person of one of the Syndicate agents in Stromgarde.","done":"Excellent, mon. That's a good start to collecting the sigils we'll need to remove Trol'kalar from Trollbane's tomb.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.8,"y":34,"n":"Zengu","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1039":{"id":1039,"t":"The Barrens Port","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.","desc":"Ratchet is the only port in the Barrens. Most likely Velinde found a trading vessel in Ratchet to take her to Blackwater Cove in Azeroth. We've had limited dealings with the goblins that run the port, but the master of the dock should have information about the comings and goings of ship passengers.\nFollow the road southeast through Ashenvale and you will find yourself in the Barrens. Watch your step, ‹name›, warriors of the Horde patrol the land. You will be safe at the port, though.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"‹race›, eh? Must admit, we don't get much of your type out here. Looking for someone, eh? Just give me a moment, I'm sure I have it written in one of my ledgers.\nLot of people travel through here, though, so just give me a moment.\nDarnassus The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":61.8,"y":39.2,"n":"Thyn'tel Bladeweaver","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.4,"y":38.5,"n":"Wharfmaster Dizzywig","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"719":{"id":719,"t":"A Dwarf and His Tools","lv":35,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Ryedol's Lucky Pick and return it to Prospector Ryedol south of Hammertoe's Dig Site.\nRyedol's Lucky Pick Shadowforge Commander 15 % , Shadowforge Darkweaver 15 % , Shadowforge Tunneler 15 % , Shadowforge Warrior 5 % and 1 more","desc":"Hey, ‹name›. Be careful 'round here. There be Dark Iron dwarves all around--looked like the Shadowforge clan.\nThey just attacked the excavation site I was workin' at--killed nearly everyone there, including my boss Hammertoe. I barely escaped with me life.\nThe site's just to the north of here, and I'm tryin' to plan a way to get some of our supplies back, especially me lucky pick.\nThink you'd be up to helpin' me out some? One of those damned Dark Iron must have my pick! Could be anyone of them.","rew":"You will receive:\nRyedol's Hammer\nExperience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Not sure what the Shadowforge were lookin' for, but they definitely had a purpose.","done":"Ye're me savior, ‹class›. I'm glad someone could teach those Shadowforge a lesson or two. Thanks for yer help.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":53.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Prospector Ryedol","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"1199":{"id":1199,"t":"Twilight Falls","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,050 experience instead of 2,550, 2.37 times as much. New rewards: Silvered Gauntlets. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a ","obj":"Bring 10 Twilight Pendants to Argent Guard Manados in Darnassus.\n10 Twilight Pendant Twilight Elementalist 80 % , Twilight Shadowmage 80 % , Twilight Loreseeker 80 % , Twilight Aquamancer 80 % and 2 more","desc":"Empowered by the ancient rites of the chaotic Old Gods the members of the Twilight's Hammer strive to bring about the return of their dark patrons and spread death and terror across the world.\nWe believe that the Twilight's Hammer has allied with the naga and are amassing in Blackfathom Deeps on the coast of Ashenvale.\nWhatever evil plan brews in the depths of the old temple must be thwarted.\nWage war on the Hammer and bring back proof of your deeds. Your efforts will be rewarded handsomely.","rew":"New in Forever: Silvered Gauntlets.\nYou will receive:\nNimbus Boots Heartwood Girdle Silvered Gauntlets\nExperience: 6,050\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Blackfathom Deeps was once an ancient night elf temple. It once housed a most powerful moonwell. Who knows what evil brews there now at the hands of the Twilight's Hammer.\nHave you made any progress in ridding their presence?","done":"You are no doubt of brave and noble blood, ‹name›. The Argent Dawn commends you for your efforts against evil.\nDarnassus Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":55.2,"y":24,"n":"Argent Guard Manados","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"97919":{"id":97919,"t":"Camping 101 first aid","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Michelle Belle in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your first aid skill to 20","desc":"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a ‹class›.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own First Aid Kit. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.4,"y":65.6,"n":"Michelle Belle","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94319":{"id":94319,"t":"Craftsmans writ draught of detect demon","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Draught of Detect Demon\nDraught of Detect Demon","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Draught of Detect Demon, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Draught of Detect Demon Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94319","cats":["crafting"]},"94239":{"id":94239,"t":"Craftsmans writ fine leather pants","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Fine Leather Pants\nFine Leather Pants","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Fine Leather Pants, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Move along, please, and try not to draw attention to us.","done":"Oh! The pants? Ah, I realized shortly after writing this that I needed a full set of clothes - new overalls included.\nIf it will get you out of my hair, I suppose I should honor the request. After all, you did make an arduous journey to find me.\nTake this, now please...\n<She gestured in a polite but firm shooing motion.>","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":34,"y":23.3,"n":"Alyce","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"1439":{"id":1439,"t":"Search for Tyranis","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Tyranis Malem in Desolace.\nTyranis' Pendant Tyranis Malem","desc":"We were brought here after the orcs slaughtered all our guards and servants. Oh, the terrible things they did to them! I thought surely they would kill us right there and then, but it became obvious they had other plans.\nTyranis attempted to speak to them. I think he wanted to impress them with his knowledge of the arcane... I'm not sure why.\nPlease, I can't leave here until I know what's happened to my brother. Find him, then come back for me when his fate is known.","rew":"Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I fear Tyranis will attempt to learn the Burning Blade's secrets and count himself among their kind if they allow it - he has always adored the power magic brings to those who are seduced by it.\nI'm not sure I could endure returning home to my family with news of Tyranis' spirit flirting with such dangers. It's a terrible enough crime among my kind to pursue such things, but to become that which we attempt to protect ourselves from, well, that's apprehensible.","done":"This is terrible! But I suppose it was necessary. If it wasn't by your hand, it would have surely been by that of my people's. I suppose I should thank you--please forgive me if it doesn't seem sincere. I mean no offense.\nWith the knowledge of my brother's fate in hand, it seems the time for my escape has come. If you are still willing, I will accept your aid in escaping this horrible place.\nWhen you are ready, we can make our way to safety.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":54.9,"y":26.1,"n":"Dalinda Malem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5519":{"id":5519,"t":"The Gordok Ogre Suit","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Bolt of Runecloth Felsteel Chest 0.9 % , Twilight Lord Everun 0 %\n8 Rugged Leather sold by Lhara\n2 Rune Thread sold by Banalash , sold by Nerrist , sold by Edna Mullby , sold by Alexandra Bolero and 4 more\nOgre Tannin Doomguard Minion , Ogre Tannin Basket , Knot Thimblejack's Cache 35 % , Gordok Warlock 0.8 % and 3 more","rew":"You will receive:\nGordok Ogre Suit\n+50 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"Need another suit, do ya? Well, I'm not going anywhere soon it seems - bring me the same things I asked for from before, and I'll make you another ogre suit.","done":"Here ya go ‹name› - put this thing on, and you'll have ten minutes to do whatever. Good luck!\nOh, and if you happen to find a key to get me out of here, BY ALL MEANS LET ME KNOW!!!\nStart Knot Thimblejack End Knot Thimblejack Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 5519\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 6,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Gordok Ogre Suit\nBring 4 Bolts of Runecloth, 8 Rugged Leather, 2 Rune Threads, and Ogre Tannin to Knot Thimblejack.\nKnot Thimblejack\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] The Gordok Ogre Suit this quest\nKnot Thimblejack","cats":["dire-maul"]},"319":{"id":319,"t":"A Favor for Evershine","lv":8,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 6 Ice Claw Bears, 8 Elder Crag Boars, and 8 Snow Leopards, and then return to Rejold Barleybrew in Brewnall Village.\nIce Claw Bear slain : 0/ 6\nElder Crag Boar slain : 0/ 8\nSnow Leopard slain : 0/ 8","desc":"I have a cask of Evershine handy, but...can you do me a favor? Brewnall village could use a hand against the wild animals that wander the nearby snows. Sometimes they wander close.\nWe're not afraid of these bears and cats and boars - no self respecting dwarf would be - but if you can take care of those animals for us, then we'd have more time for our crafting and brewing.","rew":"Experience: 525\n+75 reputation with Ironforge\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Have you taken care of those wild animals?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. It'll be nice to work our crafts without hearing so many growls and snorts outside the village.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":30.2,"y":45.7,"n":"Rejold Barleybrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"98319":{"id":98319,"t":"Secure the mountain","lv":8,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Mountaineer Cornelius in the Grizzled Den for Mountaineer Gretchen.","desc":"It's bad enough havin' a troll problem, but the mountains are filled tae the brim with wendigos! They normally keep to their own caves, but they seem tae be spreadin' like bunnies. Now they've filled the Grizzled Den north of here.\nIf we want Whitebeard's report, we're gonna need to find my partner Cornelius. The blockhead got a little too excited and charged in head first. Brave, but stupid.\nHead into the cave and see where he is. And feel free to take out some the beasts while yer at it.","done":"Ach, the fool...\nThank ye for the help, Samo. Guess we have our report.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":44,"y":57,"n":"Mountaineer Gretchen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"97279":{"id":97279,"t":"Wayward weapons","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 Abandoned Training Weapons, then return to Kzan Thornslash in the Den.\n6 Abandoned Training Weapon","desc":"With an influx of new recruits like yourself, it's been hard to keep our weapons supplied. Our weaponsmith, Kzan, is running low on training weapons and I'd like to see what kinds of skills you possess to get an idea of what I have to work with. Luckily for you, I have a solution to both.\nWhile you're out there cutting your teeth on boars, salvage six abandoned training weapons. Our failed recruits left them laying on the ground. Once you do, return them to our weaponsmith Kzan behind me in the Den.","back":"Throm'ka, ‹class›. Gorak told me I should be expecting you. It is good to see you in one piece!\nWere you able to collect the training weapons I requested?","done":"Thank you for returning these weapons, Sparkled. I will get to work repairing them for the next wave of recruits.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42,"y":68.4,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":40.4,"y":68,"n":"Kzan Thornslash","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"159":{"id":159,"t":"Juice Delivery","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Zombie Juice to Abercrombie at his shack.\nBottle of Zombie Juice\nProvided: Bottle of Zombie Juice","desc":"Here's your Zombie Juice...\n...and be careful with this stuff. It's strong enough to raise the dead!","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975","back":"I need that Zombie Juice to keep me warm on these cold, dark nights. Did you get it for me?","done":"A thousand thanks, ‹name›. You warm an old man's heart with your foolish-...I mean...with your kindness!\nHere you are, friend. Take this as a token of my gratitude.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Tavernkeep Smitts","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":28.1,"y":31.5,"n":"Abercrombie","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"79":{"id":79,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the muddy page to Commander Ebonlocke.\nMuddy Journal Pages\nProvided: Muddy Journal Pages","desc":"I followed the legend of that Stalvan character for years. When those visiting nobles were slaughtered a few years back I went with Haggard to investigate. I found these muddy pages but we were never able to link the handwriting to that crazy man in the woods. Your trail of evidence proves his guilt. Take this to Commander Ebonlocke immediately and fill her in on what you've discovered!","rew":"You will receive:\nA Bloodstained Journal Page\nExperience: 230\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"This better be good, ‹class›. Let me see what you have and tell me your tale. But by the Light, be quick about it. Darkshire's defense is my number one priority. I have not the time to squander on dead-end leads.","done":"My, you have proved yourself to be quite a detective, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Tavernkeep Smitts","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.5,"y":46.8,"n":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"239":{"id":239,"t":"Westbrook Garrison Needs Help!","lv":10,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Westbrook Garrison and speak with Deputy Rainer.","desc":"The Garrison on our western border sends word of increasing gnoll and thief activity. They're requesting we send more Stormwind soldiers... but we just don't have any to spare!\nIf you can help, we could use it. Go and speak with Deputy Rainer at the Westbrook Garrison and see what he needs done.\nThe Garrison is down the road to the west. After you cross the bridge over the small brook it will be to the right.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Marshall Dughan sent you, eh? Well you're not from the army, but if Dughan sent you then that's good enough for me!\nOur situation is, to say the least, a stressed one. I hope you can give us a hand.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":24.2,"y":74.4,"n":"Deputy Rainer","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"2879":{"id":2879,"t":"The Stave of Equinex","lv":50,"min":42,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Energize Troyas' Stave and find the Equinex Monolith.\nStave of Equinex\nProvided: Troyas' Stave","desc":"This stave might be the Stave of Equinex! The Stave of Equinex is actually a key, used to unlock the Equinex Monolith in the Ruins of Ravenwind, on the mainland west of the Dream Bough.\nFind the four flames that still burn in those ruins: Samha, Imbel, Byltan, and Lahassa. Retrieve their essence and then while standing by the Equinex Monolith, use the essences to energize the stave. If this is truly is the Stave of Equinex, you will be able to unlock the Monolith and gather a sacred artifact from it.","rew":"You will receive:\nA Sparkling Stone\nExperience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The Equinex Monolith stands silently among the ruins. What could it be holding?","done":"Holding the energized stave is almost impossible. Its power rumbles through your body.\nYou reach out to the cold surface of the Equinex Monolith...\nA small door opens, allowing you to reach in and take the artifact inside.\nBeams of light fill the area around the Equinex Monolith.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":31.8,"y":45.5,"n":"Troyas Moonbreeze","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":38.8,"y":13.2,"n":"Equinex Monolith","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"559":{"id":559,"t":"Farren's Proof","lv":32,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,550 experience instead of 2,250, 1.13 times as much.","obj":"Collect 10 Murloc Heads from the murlocs on the Western Strand for Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore.\n10 Murloc Head Torn Fin Tidehunter 40 % , Torn Fin Oracle 40 % , Torn Fin Coastrunner 40 % , Torn Fin Muckdweller 40 % and 1 more","desc":"Would you believe it, ‹name›? Redpath wasn't satisfied with all the murlocs we killed--oh now, don't be modest, you had some hand in it. Now he wants me to bring proof of the dead, hacking off cold, slimy murloc heads to submit for his approval.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550","back":"Did you get those heads for me, ‹name›?","done":"Oh for the Love of the Light... they're dripping on the ground.\nCan't stand touching those things, myself. Fish are all well and good, but when they grow legs and start walking around... Haven't eaten a fish in weeks, let me tell you, and in Southshore, that means you aren't eating much.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Lieutenant Farren Orinelle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"8959":{"id":8959,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Boots of Valor, Legplates of Valor and Spaulders of Valor.\nBoots of Valor Kirtonos the Herald 0 %\nLegplates of Valor Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nSpaulders of Valor Warchief Rend Blackhand 0 %\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together. Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nBoots of Heroism Legplates of Heroism Spaulders of Heroism\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're back, ‹name›. You must tell me all about what you've found out. But first let us arrange for your reward.","done":"I can't believe our lives are all but forfeit all because of a stupid medallion! And you're sure Anthion mentioned Bodley?\nWell, you've done your job so let's get your reward out of the way.\nEastern Plaguelands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8719":{"id":8719,"t":"Bladesing the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49,"y":37.7,"n":"Elder Bladesing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8879":{"id":8879,"t":"Large Rockets","lv":60,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will receive:\nLarge Rocket Recipes Lunar Festival Fireworks Pack","back":"Large Festival rockets light up the sky brilliantly - only the cluster rockets rival their magnificence!\nBring me coins of ancestry, <name>, and I shall share the knowledge of their creation.","done":"Very well - I accept these coins of ancestry. Here are your recipes, ‹name›. May you use them to spread Elune's glory!","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.8,"y":35.3,"n":"Fariel Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1919":{"id":1919,"t":"Report to Jennea","lv":15,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Jennea Cannon in Stormwind.","desc":"Your knowledge of the craft grows, young ‹name›. Are you now ready to begin your true lessons? Are you ready to take your place in the secret war we wage?\nIf so, then speak with Jennea Cannon, in the wizard's sanctum in the mage district of Stormwind. She has a task for you which will open your first window into the invisible world.","rew":"Experience: 110","done":"‹name›, I have a mission for you, here in the mage district. Listen closely, for there is no time to waste.\nElwynn Forest Dun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.2,"y":66.2,"n":"Zaldimar Wefhellt","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.5,"y":52.1,"n":"Magis Sparkmantle","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.4,"y":22.5,"n":"Dink","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":85.8,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9039":{"id":9039,"t":"Dreadnaught Sabatons","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Dreadnaught Sabatons if you bring him the following items: 1 Desecrated Sabatons, 12 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 2 Arcanite Bars and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Sabatons Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Gothik the Harvester 0 % in Naxxramas , Instructor Razuvious 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Arcanite Bar\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"During your battles with the Scourge in Naxxramas, should you come across desecrated battlements and wartorn plate scraps, return them to me and I shall craft for you a piece of armor worn by heroes.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreadnaught Sabatons\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Dreadnaught Sabatons.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"3119":{"id":3119,"t":"Hallowed Sigil","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Hallowed Sigil and speak to Shanda in Aldrassil.\nHallowed Sigil\nProvided: Hallowed Sigil","desc":"This sigil was given to me by a messenger from our priest trainer, Shanda. It seems Shanda would have words with you when you have a moment. Read it and bring it to her afterwards.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"It pleases me to see you've arrived so quickly, ‹name›. Welcome.\nAs you've probably heard, all of Teldrassil is stirring with the comings and goings of travelers. Even members of the Alliance have even been allowed access onto Teldrassil's boughs in order to meet with other Kaldorei who prepare for the adventures ahead.","done":"Do not concern yourself with the world below Teldrassil for now. There will be time for that later. Go now and speak to the others in Shadowglen--they can tell you more about what events have transpired. Help them in any way you can, and anytime you feel you need more training, come back to me and I will teach you what I can.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.7,"y":44.3,"n":"Conservator Ilthalaine","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":59.2,"y":40.4,"n":"Shanda","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"5679":{"id":5679,"t":"Devouring Plague","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Devouring Plague.","obj":"Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity.","desc":"Aelthalyste show our people great respect by sending them back to me for more training, and now I do the same for her tribe.\nYou return to the Undercity, ‹name›. There, in the War Quarter, she be ready to teach you more 'bout your people and their ways. Go there, and do not wait long.","rew":"You will learn: Devouring Plague","done":"I would teach you Devouring Plague if you feel you are prepared, ‹name›. A spell of no small power, it will aid you in your coming battles. Practice with it--there will be tests later.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":49.1,"y":14.6,"n":"Father Lankester","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":49.3,"y":17.1,"n":"Aelthalyste","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"95999":{"id":95999,"t":"Wanted incinerator garim","lv":25,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Broken Staff of Incinerator Gar'im to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.\nBroken Staff of Incinerator Gar'im","desc":"Wanted! Incinerator Gar'im, Leader of an orc incursion in Render's Valley. Purported to be working with the Blackrock of Stonewatch Keep.\nBeware of Incinerator Gar'im. He and his Shadowcasters are extremely dangerous. A handsome reward will to be given to any brave soul that can deliver proof of Incinerator Gar'im's demise to Magistrate Solomon.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nIncinerator's Boots Alacritous Treads Disjointed Shoes\nMoney: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What do you have there, ‹race›?","done":"Excellent work, Eraina! Incinerator Gar'im was preparing to bolster the defenses at Stonewatch Keep. With this victory, we may yet succeed in reclaiming the keep!","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.4,"y":46.2,"n":"Wanted: Incinerator Gar'im","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":30,"y":44.2,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"2239":{"id":2239,"t":"Onin's Report","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Onin's Report back to Hulfdan in Ironforge.\nOnin's Report\nProvided: Onin's Report","desc":"The Quarry? Yap, I see those monstrous armored steam tanks come by this post near every day.\nMy contacts to the east tell me that the tank starts off at Ironforge, makes a pickup at the Gol'Bolar Quarry, stops over at Kharanos to refuel and then for some blasted reason, it takes the long way around past Gnomeregan, before reaching Ironforge to drop off the shipment.\nIt's all in the report, ‹race›. Take it back to Hulfdan so he can plan the next step.","rew":"You will receive:\nBlade of Cunning\nExperience: 850","back":"Did ye enjoy the stench of leper gnome? I only ask because ye got a crazy smile on yer face.\nWhat news do ye bring from Onin?","done":"Long route? In the name o' me own beard!\nYe done good, ‹name›. Take this dagger and be gone with ye. The Circle will call upon ye again when step three be ready to be set into motion.\nWhat's step three? It comes right after step two - me putting me boot up yer backside.\nInterested?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":25.2,"y":44.5,"n":"Onin MacHammar","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.4,"y":23.5,"n":"Hulfdan Blackbeard","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1999":{"id":1999,"t":"Tools of the Trade","lv":20,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Dalaran Status Report and return it to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity.\nDalaran Status Report Ambermill Strongbox","desc":"The wizards of the Kirin Tor at Ambermill have stored away important documents pertaining to the current state of Dalaran. This we know from the admissions of one of our prisoners. Lord Varimathras has placed the duty of recovering them in the hands of the Deathstalkers.\nThis task falls to you, ‹name›. You will need some equipment, however, and the knowledge of lockpicking. Speak with Estelle Gendry, our outfitter, and ask her for a set of tools before you set out.","rew":"Experience: 1,550","back":"Have you located the documents, ‹name›?","done":"Very good, ‹name›! You have learned the fine art of lockpicking well, and faster than I could have possibly expected.\nI see that I was right to place my trust in you. Believe me, boy, I foresee that you will go far in this line of work.\nUndercity Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":83.5,"y":69.1,"n":"Mennet Carkad","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2479":{"id":2479,"t":"Hinott's Assistance","lv":26,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills and deliver the Sample of Zanzil's Mixture to Serge Hinott.\nTo get to Tarren Mill, take the Zeppelin to the Undercity and follow the road south through Silverpine and towards Hillsbrad. Follow the signs!\nSample of Zanzil's Altered Mixture\nProvided: Sample of Zanzil's Altered Mixture","desc":"Take a sample of the mixture to Serge Hinott in Tarren Mill.\nIf anyone can cure you, it's Serge. Live long enough and Serge will show you the ways of poison creation and use.","rew":"Experience: 1,050","back":"What's this???","done":"You look deliciously pale, ‹class›. And what is that foul aroma you are giving off? I must know!\nOrgrimmar Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":43,"y":53.7,"n":"Shenthul","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.6,"y":19.2,"n":"Serge Hinott","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"8799":{"id":8799,"t":"The Hero of the Day","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -5g instead of 0.","obj":"Bring 1 Deeprock Salt and 5 gold coins to the Holly Preserver machine, upon which you will receive 5 Preserved Holly.\nDeeprock Salt Garr 30 % , Setis 24.5 % , Infernal Bodyguard 24.1 % , Faulty War Golem 24 % and 4 more","desc":"Listen... I'm not really supposed to be telling you this, but since you're the hero of the day and all...\nThere's fresh holly everywhere this time of the year, but it never lasts. We've got a machine that preserves holly - it never goes bad! We use it to spice up the holiday... and profits during the summer!\nI'll let you use the preserver, but only if you're a master cook. You'll need some deeprock salt and two, three, oh let's say five gold. It'll net you a nice batch that's yours to keep.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Preserved Holly","back":"The \"Holly Preserver\" machine looks like some sort of still at first, but a careful examination of it reveals some goblin-esque changes to it. Still, your skill at cooking seems to allow you to understand how the machine works.\nThere is already fresh holly in the machine - you simply need to provide some deeprock salt and five gold coins to get the machine working.","done":"The machine lets off a little rumble and a small amount of steam as it starts working. It is not too long thereafter until it stops, heralded by another small jet of steam erupting from it. A door hatch opens, revealing a batch of preserved holly!\nOrgrimmar Stormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":53.3,"y":66.5,"n":"Kaymard Copperpinch","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":53.6,"y":67.2,"n":"Holly Preserver","e":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.1,"y":69.5,"n":"Holly Preserver","e":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.7,"y":32,"n":"Holly Preserver","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"1519":{"id":1519,"t":"Call of Earth","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 270 experience instead of 250, 1.08 times as much.","obj":"Bring 2 applications of Ritual Salve to Seer Ravenfeather in Camp Narache.\n2 Ritual Salve Bristleback Shaman 80 %","desc":"The time has come, young ‹class›. Your body ages and grows strong, and your spirit endures like the earth. I see it within you-you have wisdom already.\nThe earth guides our people, and it speaks to us, as it will to you in time. But you must be tested. If you are ready, then you shall see things only our kind know of.\nSeek out the Bristleback shamans in their ravine to the east, and take from them a salve they use in their rituals. Return to me only when you have enough for your own potion.","rew":"Experience: 270","back":"The earth is patient, and will wait for you until you are ready because she knows in time all things erode and are reborn. It is the cycle of things. Mountains become deserts. Rivers become canyons. The earth is the most stubborn and wise of all the elements.\nYou must learn patience and stamina above all things. The earth calls for you now because she feels you are ready. Consider this your rebirth if you succeed. You will never be able to go back to ignorance afterwards.","done":"Good, ‹name›. Your return here signifies that you are indeed prepared for the next step.\nOf all the elements, earth represents the foundation of all things. It is your strength, your stamina, and your patience. The Earth Mother will protect you, but only if you show her proper respect. She is the basis for life, and by observing her laws, you will gain a greater wisdom. Never forget the secrets she shares with you.\nI shall make your sapta for you now, and by accepting it, a new path will open before you.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.3,"y":76.8,"n":"Seer Ravenfeather","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8319":{"id":8319,"t":"Encrypted Twilight Texts","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Encrypted Twilight Text Twilight Prophet , Twilight Marauder 25 % , Twilight Marauder Morna 25 % , Twilight Overlord 25 % and 4 more","back":"Keep bringing me texts. We'll soon force the Twilight's Hammer out of Silithus.","done":"Excellent work! I'll put a good word in for you.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"479":{"id":479,"t":"Ambermill Investigations","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Obtain 8 Dalaran Pendants for Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.\n8 Dalaran Pendant Dalaran Conjuror 80 % , Dalaran Mage 80 % , Dalaran Protector 80 %","desc":"Dalar is attempting to locate the source of the wizards' spellcasting. For now, we'll have to slow their progress in any way we can...\nThe conjurers, mages and protectors are no doubt carrying the pendants. Remove and retrieve them.\nTake the main road south and the eastern fork into Ambermill.","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"We must hurry, their plans must not come to fruition, or we may lose our hold on Silverpine Forest.","done":"Dalar has found that the weaving is quite far along, despite the setback.\nA wizard of great power is guiding the magic energy. He must be stopped quickly.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44,"y":40.9,"n":"Shadow Priest Allister","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"84399":{"id":84399,"t":"Ka boom","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Ka-Boom!","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nKa-Boom! (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.6,"y":79.4,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"399":{"id":399,"t":"Humble Beginnings","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to Baros Alexston's house in Westfall and search for his compass, then return it to him in Cathedral Square of Stormwind.\nA Simple Compass Alexston's Chest","desc":"It seems an eternity since I was a boy working the farm in Westfall. They say you can never go back, and it's true. Doubly true in my case, my family's home has been burned down and taken over by thieves.\nI have spoken with my father about the fate of some of my possessions, including my first compass. He was unable to save them. However, he also says that they should be hidden away on the farm.\nYou'll find the Alexston Farmstead west of Sentinel Hill. Perhaps you could go and retrieve it for me?","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›! Did you have any luck?","done":"Oh, thank you, ‹name›! It's of no practical use to me, but the sentimental value... Needless to say, thank you for bringing this to me... at some cost to your own well-being, not to mention the time it took to go all the way down to Westfall. You have my gratitude, and have this as a token of my thanks.\nStormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":57.7,"y":47.9,"n":"Baros Alexston","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"8079":{"id":8079,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Vindicator's Breastplate","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker a Primal Hakkari Kossack. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.\nJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Kossack\nReach 21000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"The vindicator's symbol of power is the breastplate. It is forged with powerful mojo. It is trusted only to those we revere. It is the Zandalar symbol of vengeance.\nTo become a vindicator is to become vengeance. Take the Paragons of Power we need from Zul'Gurub. Bring them to us. We will take the mojo stolen from us. We will make the minions of Hakkar pay. We will reward you with the vindicator's breastplate.\nGo. Be our vengeance, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Vindicator's Breastplate\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Your presence means victory? Do you have the Paragons of Power? Tell me of the vengeance you have wrought today!","done":"You are to be revered for your deeds. The tribe rewards its heroes. Zul'Gurub has tasted Zandalar vengeance like never before.\nYour deeds will herald the deeds of others to come. They will look upon you as a sign of real power. They will look upon you as vengeance personified!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8239":{"id":8239,"t":"Sandfury, Skullsplitter, and Bloodscalp Coins","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Sandfury Coin Hakkari Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Blood Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more\nSkullsplitter Coin Hakkari Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Blood Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more\nBloodscalp Coin Hakkari Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Blood Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"I seek the Paragons of Power known as the Coins of the Tribes. They are the currency used by the various denizens of Zul'Gurub, and each is imbued with subtle but powerful mojo.\nThere are nine distinct kinds to be found. Some are sought after by my compatriots for various armors they offer Zandalar heroes. Should you have any extra, I will trade you one of our Honor Tokens for a set of three. You may use the Tokens with Rin'wosho the Trader; he offers our heroes special items for them.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Honor Token\nExperience: 650\n+25 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"I seek the Paragons of Power known as the Coins of the Tribes. They are the currency used by the various denizens of Zul'Gurub, and each is imbued with subtle but powerful mojo.\nThere are nine distinct kinds to be found. Should you have any extra, I will trade you one of our Honor Tokens for a set of three. You may use the Tokens with Rin'wosho the Trader; he offers our heroes special items for them.","done":"Excellent - this set of coins will make a fine addition to our growing collection... one that we will use in the tribe's defense against the rise of the Blood God. You've earned this Honor Token, ‹name›, as well as the thanks of the tribe!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.5,"y":15.8,"n":"Vinchaxa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3519":{"id":3519,"t":"A Friend in Need","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Dirania Silvershine in Shadowglen.","desc":"Ughhh... I was bitten very badly by a spider named Githyiss the Vile while exploring the spider cave very close to here. I am sure I have been seriously poisoned; you must help me.\nPlease tell Dirania Silvershine. She will be able to help me.\nHurry... I'm so dizzy...","rew":"Experience: 90\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Oh dear; I was wondering why I hadn't seen Iverron yet today. And I've always warned him about those spiders...","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":54.6,"y":33,"n":"Iverron","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":42,"n":"Dirania Silvershine","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"2159":{"id":2159,"t":"Dolanaar Delivery","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Dolanaar Delivery to Innkeeper Keldamyr.\nDolanaar Delivery\nProvided: Dolanaar Delivery","desc":"Greetings, young ‹class›. Can you offer me aid? I have a package of herbs that I must deliver to the town of Dolanaar. But I still have business with the druids of Shadowglen and cannot yet leave.\nCan you deliver this package for me? It must be sent to Innkeeper Keldamyr, at the Dolanaar inn. It lies along the road, to the south.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Darnassian Bleu 5 Refreshing Spring Water\nExperience: 110\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","back":"How might I be of service to you, young one? Are you here to rest in the inn? Do you require a hearthstone?","done":"Ah yes, the delivery of herbs from Shadowglen. It is a shame Porthannius could not bring it himself, for we have much to discuss, he and I. But I am glad to get the herbs nonetheless, and I am glad you came.\nWhile you are here, please, rest yourself. Heroes must keep their strength and spirits high, and must find rest and solace whenever they may. For to neglect one's peace of body and mind is a sure path to failure.\nSo... rest.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":61.2,"y":47.6,"n":"Porthannius","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.6,"y":59.8,"n":"Innkeeper Keldamyr","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"2399":{"id":2399,"t":"The Sprouted Fronds","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Sprouted Frond\nExperience: 85\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"The fronds Denalan planted within his garden have sprouted and grown. They tremble, eager to be picked....","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.7,"y":68.6,"n":"Sprouted Frond","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"879":{"id":879,"t":"Betrayal from Within","lv":25,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Nak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane and bring their skulls to Mangletooth at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.\nKuz's Skull Kuz\nNak's Skull Nak\nLok's Skull Lok Orcbane","desc":"Three of my tribe came out of the Kraul to lead the raids against the Horde, ‹race›. <snort> They are ruthless and cunning, and if you defeat them, then your Crossroads and even most of the Barrens will learn peace... <snort> at least from the Razormane tribe. <snort>\nNak, Kuz, and Lok Orcbane are the ones you seek. They are far to the south of the Barrens. One is a spell caster, another a tracker, and their leader, the one called Orcbane, <snort> a warrior. Kill them, ‹race›, like they have killed me.","rew":"Experience: 1,500\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How goes your hunt, ‹race›? <snort>\nThork thinks he knows the truth about who leads the raids against his people, <snort> but he shall learn how wrong he is if you are successful.\nMy death is inescapable, but you have caused great pain to my enemies, so Mangletooth regrets nothing. <snort>","done":"It is done then. Better it ends this way, says Mangletooth. <snort> They should have <snort> made sure I was dead when they turned their backs on me instead of leaving <snort> me here in this forsaken cage.\nThere is but one task left for you to finish, ‹race›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.5,"y":59.3,"n":"Mangletooth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"7839":{"id":7839,"t":"Vilebranch Hooligans","lv":48,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Smith Slagtree at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to find Slagtree's Lost Tools. Return to him once this task is complete.\nYou recall Smith Slagtree mentioning that the tools might be at one of the Vilebranch temples in the northeastern region of the Hinterlands. You should also check Skulk Rock.\nSlagtree's Lost Tools Slagtree's Lost Tools","desc":"Vilebranch scum invaded our village and stole my tools! I have backup tools but the set they stole was a gift given to me by a kind hearted gnome that saved my life when I was a young orc.\nI want those tools back, ‹name› - they mean the world to me.\nMarkhor reported that the tools were spotted near the Agol'watha and Shaol'watha temples.\nThose temples are in the northeastern region of the Hinterlands.\nRecover my tools!","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"Watch out for the Vilebranch trolls of the region, ‹name›. They are ruthless, murderous filth.","done":"My tools! You found them! Oh glorious day! Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":77.2,"y":80.1,"n":"Smith Slagtree","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1119":{"id":1119,"t":"Zanzil's Mixture and a Fool's Stout","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Fool's Stout back to Kravel in the Shimmering Flats.\nFool's Stout\nProvided: Fool's Stout","desc":"I figured out how to use Zanzil's mixture with stout to make a powerful libation. A Fool's Stout. I think it'll be just what Kravel needs, but try it out and let me know how it works.\nAnd ‹name›, don't keep this stuff too long without using it. Zanzil's mixture has a weird effect on the stout's yeast, kicking it into high gear. So it won't stay fresh forever.","rew":"Experience: 3,750","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Was Fizzlebub able to help us?","done":"Wonderful! Fizzlebub came through! I'll remember that next time I see him.\nAnd thank you, ‹name›. You're doing a great job, and we both stand to make a lot of money from this...\nStranglethorn Vale Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.1,"y":77.2,"n":"Crank Fizzlebub","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1359":{"id":1359,"t":"Zinge's Delivery","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Wolf Heart Samples to Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity.\nWolf Heart Samples\nProvided: Wolf Heart Samples","desc":"The wolf hearts you acquired possess a quality unseen in similar specimens. There is a toxicity to them that should be deadly to the very wolves in which the hearts beat!\nIt's quite incredible, and we must study it further. I kept a few samples of the hearts acquired. Take them to my colleague, Apothecary Zinge. You will find her in our headquarters in the Undercity.","rew":"Experience: 110\n+10 reputation with Undercity","back":"You have something for me?","done":"Ah yes, the heart samples of which Renferrel spoke. I am eager to experiment with these... it is always of interest to the Royal Apothecary Society when new forms of toxins are discovered.\nSilverpine Forest Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":50.1,"y":68,"n":"Apothecary Zinge","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"959":{"id":959,"t":"Trouble at the Docks","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,650 experience instead of 1,350, 1.96 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Crane Operator Bigglefuzz in Ratchet wants you to retrieve the bottle of 99-Year-Old Port from Mad Magglish who is hiding in the Wailing Caverns.\n99-Year-Old Port Mad Magglish","desc":"Oops!\nHad a little mishap, as you can see! The morning cargo shipment from Booty Bay was huge. Huge I say! Never seen so many crates. Well, I was trying to expedite things so I started unloading a bit more than I could handle. That's when everything came tumbling down.\nBefore I knew what was going on, I saw that menace, Mad Magglish, go running off with a bottle of 99-year-old port. Chased him all the way to Wailing Caverns. No way I was going in there.\nMaybe you're brave enough to find him?","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"The dockmaster has been on my case ever since Mad Magglish made off with that 99-year-old port. I guess that bottle was intended as a gift for Gazlowe from none other than Baron Revilgaz himself.\nIf you're brave enough and patient enough to seek out Mad Magglish and get that port back, I'll see to it you get a nice reward.","done":"Superb! And just as I was about to lose my job too! I will see to it that Gazlowe gets this gift immediately.\nThank you, ‹name›. Nicely done, I say!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.1,"y":37.6,"n":"Crane Operator Bigglefuzz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"1599":{"id":1599,"t":"Beginnings","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Feather Charms to Alamar Grimm in Anvilmar.\n3 Feather Charm Frostmane Novice 80 %","desc":"You must be the new warlock everyone's been whispering about. Must be someone's taken a liking to you if they've asked me to take time away from my research to start your training.\nDon't worry, I won't hold it against you.\nThe simplest of the summoning spells you will learn is that of the imp. Before I impart this to you, however, you must prove that you have the necessary magical and physical ability.\nBring me three feather charms from the frostmane novices from the cave to the southwest.","rew":"You will learn: Summon Imp\nExperience: 360\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Those feather charms the novices carry have some sort of magical power to them. It will be interesting to research them. I wouldn't have expected it from the trolls.","done":"Very good, very good! You've done well, ‹name›. Perhaps the interest that is being shown in you is deserved, after all.\nThat'll be for the others to decide--assuming your imp doesn't overpower you and nip your career in the bud. For now, I'm satisfied that you'll probably survive your first few months as a warlock.\nA word about the imp, ‹name›. As a gnome knows, don't let its size fool you, its magic can be very dangerous.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.6,"y":66.1,"n":"Alamar Grimm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"92479":{"id":92479,"t":"A scribbled letter","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Read the Scribbled Letter and speak to Tordrin Stemblade in Northshire Abbey.\nProvided: Scribbled Letter","desc":"I was asked to bring this to your attention as soon as you returned from the kobold camps, ‹name›. It appears to be a letter sealed with the mark of Tordrin Stemblade, our local hunter trainer. Take a moment to read it before you go about any other business here in the Abbey.","back":"Ah, ye got me letter, Busch... good.\nTime was when ye'd not catch a ‹race› dead wit' a bow in their hand--no more, I guess. It's good for Stormwind, but bad for the kobolds and man eatin' beasts in the area.","done":"Get yerself squared away, learn the lay o' the land, and come back to me whenever you need training. I'll be here night or day.\nThis land is grown' more dangerous, and as ye meet other folk, I think ye'll find they all have problems they could use some help with--help a skilled ‹class› can give 'em. Good luck.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.8,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":51.2,"y":40.8,"n":"Tordrin Sternblade","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1679":{"id":1679,"t":"Muren Stormpike","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Muren Stormpike.","desc":"Hello, warrior! You show a lot of promise, but you still need to learn some tricks and Muren Stormpike is just the dwarf to teach you.\nYou can find Muren at the Hall of Arms in the Military Ward of Ironforge. Talk to him when you're ready to learn what it is to be a warrior.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Ah, ‹name›. I heard the warriors of Dun Morogh bouncing your name around. I hope you haven't spent all your time in the breweries!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.4,"y":52.6,"n":"Granis Swiftaxe","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.4,"y":35.6,"n":"Muren Stormpike","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1839":{"id":1839,"t":"Ula'elek and the Brutal Gauntlets","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ula'elek in Durotar.","desc":"The troll smith Ula'elek will craft for you the brutal gauntlets. He dwells in Durotar, in Sen'jin Village with his Darkspear brethren, and he awaits your coming.","rew":"Experience: 1,200","done":"Greetings, ‹name›. Old Thun'grim sent word to me of your coming, but had he kept silent your presence here would not have surprised me.\nThe spirits follow your progress, young warrior, and they tell me that many foes have fallen before you.\nThe Barrens Durotar","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":57.2,"y":30.3,"n":"Thun'grim Firegaze","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":56.3,"y":74.3,"n":"Ula'elek","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8399":{"id":8399,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Good work, ‹name›. Thanks to you, our natural defenses in Ashenvale will remain intact for another day.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]}});